meta {
  name: OAuth GitHub Callback
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/oauth/github/callback
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  GitHub OAuth callback handler. Called after user grants consent.
  Flow:
    1. Receives authorization code from GitHub via Supabase redirect.
    2. Exchanges code for a Supabase session via `exchangeCodeForSession()` (PKCE).
    3. Enforces email verification gate (PRD §5.1): if email_confirmed_at is null, session is deleted and 401 is returned.
    4. Supabase handles GitHub email fallback (private emails) natively.
    5. New users get a tenant auto-provisioned via the Supabase database trigger `handle_verified_user`.
    6. Redirects to {FRONTEND_URL}/oauth-callback with access_token and refresh_token as query params.
  Returns: HTTP 302 to frontend on success, or 302 with error param if failed.
  Internal classification: PUBLIC (no auth token required).
}
